Package: [[name]]
# Not [[version]]: that is the raw Maven version, and apt compares on this line. This is the
# agent module's version with -SNAPSHOT rewritten to ~SNAPSHOT, which sorts below the release
# rather than above it.
Version: [[agent.package.version]]
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Michael Schnell <michael@fuin.org>
Homepage: https://github.com/porelo-ai/porelo
Depends: porelo
# No 'Provides: porelo-agent': that is what offers an agent to a person, and the stub is only for the suite.
Description: [[description]] [[agent.cli.version]]
 Installs its program under /usr/lib and one description file into
 /usr/share/porelo/agents.d that names it, which is where the porelo binary
 looks for agents. Nothing else is registered: porelo asks the program the
 description names to describe itself, so installing this package is enough.
 .
 The package version is this agent's own version, independent of Porelo's release
 line. The agent CLI version it installs is on the Description line above, so
 "dpkg -s porelo-agent-claude" answers what an image build will fetch without
 consulting the definition.
